      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`more_itertools.chunked` keeps the leftover items. It returns them as a final, shorter chunk and doesn't pad or drop them.\n\n```python\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7]]\n```\n\nEach chunk is a list. If you need every chunk to be the same length, you have two options:\n\n- **`strict=True`**: raises `ValueError` if the last chunk is short. This needs `more_itertools` 6.0 or later.\n- **`more_itertools.grouper`** (older versions called it `ichunked` or `zip_longest`-style): pads the last chunk with a fill value. Use `grouper(iterable, n, incomplete='fill', fillvalue=None)`. `incomplete` can also be `'strict'` or `'ignore'`. `'ignore'` drops the leftovers.\n\nI'm going from memory here and didn't check the installed version. The argument order of `grouper` changed across releases, so check the docs for your version before relying on it.",
